## 7. The 20 Platform Distribution Masks & 40 Golden Rules

MAXXX OS does not treat all platforms equally. It recognizes 4 strategic divisions and enforces 2 strict, hard-coded linter rules per platform (totaling 40 rules).

### [TECH DIVISION] (Focus: Engineers, Builders, Open Source)

1. **X (Twitter):** Max 280 characters. No raw URLs in the first tweet of a thread.
2. **X (Twitter):** Must start with a contrarian hook or strong data point.
3. **LinkedIn:** Strict 800–1,200 character limit.
4. **LinkedIn:** Must contain at least 3 double-spaced line breaks for readability.
5. **GitHub:** Must be valid Markdown. All code snippets wrapped in ``` blocks.
6. **GitHub:** README must include clear "Installation" and "Usage" sections.
7. **Dev.to:** Must contain at least one H2 (##) and one H3 (###) heading.
8. **Dev.to:** Must include at least one code block if the topic is technical.
9. **Medium:** Paragraphs must not exceed 4 sentences. Sub-headers every 150 words.
10. **Medium:** Must include a high-quality featured image with descriptive alt-text.
11. **Peerlist:** Max 400 characters. Focus strictly on "what I built" and "tech stack".
12. **Peerlist:** Must tag the specific tools/frameworks used in the project.
13. **Reddit:** Zero blatant self-promotion in the first 2 sentences. Must provide standalone value.
14. **Reddit:** Title must not use clickbait; must clearly state the technical problem solved.
15. **LeetCode:** Solution must include Time and Space Complexity (Big O) notes.
16. **LeetCode:** Code must be heavily commented explaining the algorithmic logic.
17. **Hashnode:** Must include a canonical URL tag if cross-posting from a personal domain.
18. **Hashnode:** Must select at least 3 relevant tags from the Hashnode ecosystem.
19. **HackerNews:** Title must be plain text, no clickbait, no exclamation marks.
20. **HackerNews:** "Show HN" posts must include a direct, working link to the project.

### [MEDIA DIVISION] (Focus: Broad Audience, Visuals, Storytelling)

21. **Instagram:** Caption must end with a block of 5-10 relevant hashtags.
22. **Instagram:** First line must be a "punchy" hook under 50 characters.
23. **YouTube:** Description must include timestamp links (e.g., 0:00 Intro) if video > 2 mins.
24. **YouTube:** Must include a clear Channel CTA (Call to Action) at the end.
25. **Quora:** Answer must be >300 words and cite at least one authoritative source.
26. **Quora:** Must directly answer the question in the very first sentence.
27. **LinkedOut:** Must contain a paradoxical career insight or satirical humor. No corporate jargon.
28. **LinkedOut:** Must use a specific narrative structure (Setup -> Twist -> Punchline).
29. **Threads:** Max 500 characters. Must be conversational, ending with a question.
30. **Threads:** No external links allowed in the main post; must be placed in the first reply.
31. **Facebook:** Tone must be conversational and community-focused. No aggressive sales pitches.
32. **Facebook:** Must include an engaging visual (image/video) to trigger algorithmic reach.
33. **Substack:** Must include a clear subscriber CTA (e.g., "Subscribe for more").
34. **Substack:** Editorial depth required: minimum 3 distinct sections.
35. **Telegram:** Must use Markdown formatting for bolding key insights.
36. **Telegram:** Must include direct, un-shortened links for trust.

### [MAFIA & SAAS DIVISION] (Focus: High-Leverage, B2B, Product Launches)

37. **ProductHunt:** Pitch must be under 100 words. Must include "Maker's note" perspective.
38. **ProductHunt:** Must explicitly ask for specific feedback, not just "upvotes".
39. **Discord:** Code snippets must use language-specific syntax highlighting (e.g., ```python).
40. **Discord:** Must use appropriate role tags (e.g., @devs) ONLY if critical; no spam tagging.

